; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR SIMPLE-CALC 8  -  eight significant digits; the arithmetic is
; native 1802 called by $F1 RUNMC                          (VM1 @ $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Companion to Simple-Calc-5 (same keys, same rules, three more digits).
; Needs firmware with RUNMC $F1, PRINTSTR $C1 and GETSTR $C2; built and
; verified against V0061.30.
;
;   > 1/7              = 0.14285714
;   > 123456.78*9      = 1111111     (1111111.02 to 8 digits)
;   > 2+3*4            = 20          left to right, like a pocket calculator
;   > *2               = 40          a line starting + * / uses the last answer
;   > -2.5*4           = -10         a leading - is a negative number
;   > 99999999*99999999 = 9.9999998E15
;   > 5/0              = Err         the last answer is kept
;   Esc, or Enter on an empty line, quits.  x also means times.
;
; NUMBERS carry 8 significant digits and a decimal exponent; every result is
; the exact answer ROUNDED HALF-UP to 8 digits (so 1/3*3 = 0.99999999, as on a
; pocket calculator). Up to 9.9999999E99; smaller than 1E-99 becomes 0.
; Plain display for integers of up to 12 digits and up to 12 decimal places,
; d.ddddddd E x otherwise.
;
; THE SPLIT. The STELLAR program ($4000-$4326) reads the line, keeps the
; running answer and prints. All the arithmetic is ONE native routine at
; $4800 (Firmware-Math/calc8_native.asm, 770 bytes), entered with RUNMC $4800
; and an operation letter at $4D30: N (round a typed number), + - * /.
; Numbers are held ONE DECIMAL DIGIT PER BYTE, so the parser writes digits
; straight into the native work area and the printer reads them back - no
; binary/decimal conversion anywhere. The native code does schoolbook
; arithmetic that is exact up to one final rounding: add/subtract at the true
; alignment, a full 16-digit product, and long division to 10 digits.
;
; RECORDS (page $4D): NA $4D00 the running answer, NB $4D10 the number just
; typed, ANS $4D20 the last answer. 10 bytes each: sign, exponent+$80, eight
; digits (most significant first); value = digits x 10^exponent. $4D30
; operation, $4D31 status (0 ok, 1 divide by zero, 2 too big), $4D32-34 the
; parser's raw exponent/count/sign, $4D40 work area, $4D80/$4D90 divide.
; Input line at $4E00.
;
; RUNMC CONVENTION (see RUNMC-Test.lst / gol_native.asm): absolute address,
; return with D5, RA avoided, SEX R2 before returning. Inside, the native code
; calls its own subroutines through the firmware's SCRT (D4/D5); that touches
; only R2, R3, R6 and D. The longest native call (a divide) is ~25,000 1802
; instructions - about a tenth of a second - and does not yield to other VMs.
;
; VERIFICATION (real V0061.30 image, cold boot):
;   Firmware-Math/calc8_native_test.py - the native routine alone, 3018 random + hand cases vs the model, 0 wrong.
;   Firmware-Math/simplecalc8_verify.py - the whole program against an
;   exact-fraction model, character for character: 81 set lines + 400 random expressions, 0 wrong.
;
; HARDWARE-VERIFIED on the Elf2K, 2026-09-24, on firmware V0061.33 - Craig: "works
; very well". The first app whose arithmetic runs as native 1802 through RUNMC.
;
; 277 STELLAR commands, $4000-$4326 (807 bytes); native code $4800-$4B01.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START                              Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A                    Ten
; D 4005 11 0E 0D 20    LOADXI R14 0D20                    The last answer starts as +0: sign 0, exponent $80,
; D 4009 32 0E 00 80    COPYMX2I R14 0080
; D 400D 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4011 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 4015 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4019 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 401D 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4021 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 4025 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4029 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000                  eight zero digits (the pre-pass does not clear RAM)
; D 402D 11 0E 0C 00    LOADXI R14 0C00
; D 4031 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       The banner
; PROMPT:
; D 4033 11 0E 0B 40    LOADXI R14 0B40
; D 4037 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       >
; D 4039 11 0C 0E 00    LOADXI R12 0E00
; D 403D 11 0D 0E 00    LOADXI R13 0E00
; D 4041 BD 01 1D       CALL GETL                          Read a line (echoed; backspace works; a lone ESC first quits)
; D 4044 11 0C 0E 00    LOADXI R12 0E00                    Back to the start of it
; D 4048 BD 01 72       CALL SKIPSP
; D 404B 8C 00          TESTXZ R0                          An empty line quits
; D 404D A0 01 16       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 4050 86 00 00 2B    TESTXI R0 002B                     A line that starts with + * / carries on
; D 4054 A0 00 81       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 4057 86 00 00 2A    TESTXI R0 002A                     from the last answer
; D 405B A0 00 81       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 405E 86 00 00 2F    TESTXI R0 002F
; D 4062 A0 00 81       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 4065 BD 01 93       CALL PARSE                         The first number -> NB
; D 4068 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10                         No digits: not a number
; D 406A A0 00 FE       IFTRUEI SYNERR
; D 406D BD 01 86       CALL STATUS                        Too big to hold?
; D 4070 A1 01 07       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 4073 11 0D 0D 10    LOADXI R13 0D10                    It becomes the running answer NA
; D 4077 11 0E 0D 00    LOADXI R14 0D00
; D 407B 3B DE 0A       COPYMXMY R13 R14 0A                10-byte record
; D 407E B0 00 8C       GAL OPLOOP
; USEANS:
; D 4081 11 0D 0D 20    LOADXI R13 0D20                    Load the last answer
; D 4085 11 0E 0D 00    LOADXI R14 0D00
; D 4089 3B DE 0A       COPYMXMY R13 R14 0A                10-byte record
; OPLOOP:
; D 408C BD 01 72       CALL SKIPSP
; D 408F 8C 00          TESTXZ R0                          End of the line: show the answer
; D 4091 A0 00 E7       IFTRUEI SHOW
; D 4094 23 00 09       COPYXY R0 -> R9                    R9 = the operator
; D 4097 86 09 00 2B    TESTXI R9 002B
; D 409B A0 00 BE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 409E 86 09 00 2D    TESTXI R9 002D
; D 40A2 A0 00 BE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 40A5 86 09 00 2A    TESTXI R9 002A
; D 40A9 A0 00 BE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 40AC 86 09 00 2F    TESTXI R9 002F
; D 40B0 A0 00 BE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 40B3 86 09 00 78    TESTXI R9 0078                     x means times
; D 40B7 A1 00 FE       IFFALSEI SYNERR
; D 40BA 11 09 00 2A    LOADXI R9 002A
; OPOK:
; D 40BE 42 0C          INCX R12                           Past the operator
; D 40C0 BD 01 72       CALL SKIPSP
; D 40C3 BD 01 93       CALL PARSE                         The next number -> NB
; D 40C6 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 40C8 A0 00 FE       IFTRUEI SYNERR
; D 40CB BD 01 86       CALL STATUS
; D 40CE A1 01 07       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 40D1 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 40D5 22 09          COPYXA R9 -> Acc                   The operation letter for the native code
; D 40D7 2F 0E 0D 30    WRITEIDX R14 0D30
; D 40DB F1 48 00       RUNMC 4800                         NA = NA op NB, in raw 1802
; D 40DE BD 01 86       CALL STATUS                        Divide by zero, or too big?
; D 40E1 A1 01 07       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 40E4 B0 00 8C       GAL OPLOOP
; SHOW:
; D 40E7 11 0D 0D 00    LOADXI R13 0D00                    Keep it as the last answer
; D 40EB 11 0E 0D 20    LOADXI R14 0D20
; D 40EF 3B DE 0A       COPYMXMY R13 R14 0A                10-byte record
; D 40F2 11 0E 0B 48    LOADXI R14 0B48
; D 40F6 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                        =
; D 40F8 BD 02 38       CALL PRINTNUM
; D 40FB B0 00 33       GAL PROMPT
; SYNERR:
; D 40FE 11 0E 0B 58    LOADXI R14 0B58
; D 4102 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                        = ?  (the last answer is kept)
; D 4104 B0 00 33       GAL PROMPT
; MATHERR:
; D 4107 11 0E 0B 48    LOADXI R14 0B48
; D 410B C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 410D 11 0E 0B 50    LOADXI R14 0B50
; D 4111 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       Err
; D 4113 B0 00 33       GAL PROMPT
; QUIT:
; D 4116 11 0E 0B 60    LOADXI R14 0B60
; D 411A C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 411C 00             HALT
; GETL:
; GETLK:
; D 411D CB             SERIN                              the first key
; D 411E 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B
; D 4121 A1 01 35       IFFALSEI GETLN
; D 4124 BD 01 59       CALL GETLW                         ESC: an arrow following?
; D 4127 A1 01 16       IFFALSEI QUIT                      no: ESC on its own quits
; D 412A CB             SERIN                              an arrow (ESC [ x): its two bytes are thrown away
; D 412B BD 01 59       CALL GETLW
; D 412E A1 01 1D       IFFALSEI GETLK
; D 4131 CB             SERIN
; D 4132 B0 01 1D       GAL GETLK
; GETLN:
; D 4135 81 00 0D       TESTAI 000D
; D 4138 A1 01 43       IFFALSEI GETLC
; D 413B 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 413E 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)      Enter alone: the empty line
; D 4141 BE 00          RETURN
; GETLC:
; D 4143 81 00 08       TESTAI 0008
; D 4146 A0 01 1D       IFTRUEI GETLK                      nothing to rub out yet
; D 4149 81 00 7F       TESTAI 007F
; D 414C A0 01 1D       IFTRUEI GETLK
; D 414F C9             SEROUT                             the echo
; D 4150 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)
; D 4153 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4155 C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     the rest of the line (Backspace can rub out the first key too)
; D 4157 BE 00          RETURN
; GETLW:
; D 4159 72 09          PUSHX R9
; D 415B 11 09 00 08    LOADXI R9 0008
; GETLW1:
; D 415F CC             SERST
; D 4160 A0 01 6A       IFTRUEI GETLW2
; D 4163 43 09          DECX R9
; D 4165 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 4167 A1 01 5F       IFFALSEI GETLW1
; GETLW2:
; D 416A 73 09          POPX R9
; D 416C CC             SERST                              Test: a key is waiting
; D 416D BE 00          RETURN
; D 416F F0 00 00       BREAK                              End of program
; SKIPSP:
; D 4172 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 4176 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 4178 86 00 00 20    TESTXI R0 0020
; D 417C A1 01 84       IFFALSEI SKR
; D 417F 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4181 B0 01 72       GAL SKIPSP
; SKR:
; D 4184 BE 00          RETURN
; STATUS:
; D 4186 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 418A 2E 0E 0D 31    READIDX R14 0D31
; D 418E 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4191 BE 00          RETURN
; PARSE:
; D 4193 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; D 4197 11 05 00 00    LOADXI R5 0000
; D 419B 11 06 00 80    LOADXI R6 0080
; D 419F 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; D 41A3 11 0A 00 00    LOADXI R10 0000
; D 41A7 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 41AB 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 41AD 86 00 00 2D    TESTXI R0 002D                     A leading minus
; D 41B1 A1 01 BA       IFFALSEI PLOOP
; D 41B4 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001
; D 41B8 42 0C          INCX R12
; PLOOP:
; D 41BA 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 41BE 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 41C0 86 00 00 2E    TESTXI R0 002E
; D 41C4 A1 01 D5       IFFALSEI PDIG
; D 41C7 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          A second point ends the number
; D 41C9 A1 02 16       IFFALSEI PEND
; D 41CC 11 08 00 01    LOADXI R8 0001                     Digits from here on are fraction
; D 41D0 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 41D2 B0 01 BA       GAL PLOOP
; PDIG:
; D 41D5 53 00 00 30    SUBXI R0 0030                      A digit is '0'..'9': c-'0' < 10
; D 41D9 89 0F          TESTLXY R0 < R15
; D 41DB A1 02 16       IFFALSEI PEND
; D 41DE 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 41E0 11 0A 00 01    LOADXI R10 0001                    Seen a digit
; D 41E4 8C 05          TESTXZ R5                          A leading zero is not kept
; D 41E6 A1 01 F1       IFFALSEI PKEEP
; D 41E9 8C 00          TESTXZ R0
; D 41EB A1 01 F1       IFFALSEI PKEEP
; D 41EE B0 02 02       GAL PFRAC                          but after the point it still moves the exponent
; PKEEP:
; D 41F1 11 0E 00 14    LOADXI R14 0014                    Keep up to 20 digits
; D 41F5 89 5E          TESTLXY R5 < R14
; D 41F7 A1 02 0C       IFFALSEI PFULL
; D 41FA 22 00          COPYXA R0 -> Acc
; D 41FC 2F 05 0D 40    WRITEIDX R5 0D40                   W[k] = the digit
; D 4200 42 05          INCX R5
; PFRAC:
; D 4202 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          After the point each digit is a tenth
; D 4204 A0 01 BA       IFTRUEI PLOOP
; D 4207 43 06          DECX R6
; D 4209 B0 01 BA       GAL PLOOP
; PFULL:
; D 420C 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          A dropped digit before the point is a x10
; D 420E A1 01 BA       IFFALSEI PLOOP
; D 4211 42 06          INCX R6
; D 4213 B0 01 BA       GAL PLOOP
; PEND:
; D 4216 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000                    Hand the raw digits to the native code
; D 421A 22 05          COPYXA R5 -> Acc
; D 421C 2F 0E 0D 33    WRITEIDX R14 0D33
; D 4220 22 06          COPYXA R6 -> Acc
; D 4222 2F 0E 0D 32    WRITEIDX R14 0D32
; D 4226 22 04          COPYXA R4 -> Acc
; D 4228 2F 0E 0D 34    WRITEIDX R14 0D34
; D 422C 10 00 4E       LOADAI 004E
; D 422F 2F 0E 0D 30    WRITEIDX R14 0D30
; D 4233 F1 48 00       RUNMC 4800                         Round to 8 digits -> NB
; D 4236 BE 00          RETURN
; PRINTNUM:
; D 4238 11 07 00 08    LOADXI R7 0008
; PNT:
; D 423C 8C 07          TESTXZ R7                          All eight zero: the number is 0
; D 423E A0 03 23       IFTRUEI PNZERO
; D 4241 43 07          DECX R7
; D 4243 2E 07 0D 02    READIDX R7 0D02                    Drop trailing zeros
; D 4247 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 424A A0 02 3C       IFTRUEI PNT
; D 424D 42 07          INCX R7
; D 424F 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4253 2E 0E 0D 00    READIDX R14 0D00                   The sign
; D 4257 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 425A A0 02 5F       IFTRUEI PN1
; D 425D CA 2D          SEROUTI 2D '-'
; PN1:
; D 425F 2E 0E 0D 01    READIDX R14 0D01                   e = exponent + 8 - n
; D 4263 21 03          COPYAX Acc -> R3
; D 4265 52 03 00 08    ADDXI R3 0008
; D 4269 51 37 03       SUBXYZ R3 - R7 -> R3
; D 426C 50 73 08       ADDXYZ R7 + R3 -> R8               p = n + e
; D 426F 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 4273 11 0E 00 80    LOADXI R14 0080
; D 4277 88 3E          TESTGXY R3 >= R14                  e >= 0: plain if p <= 12
; D 4279 A1 02 88       IFFALSEI PNNEG
; D 427C 11 0E 00 8C    LOADXI R14 008C
; D 4280 88 E8          TESTGXY R14 >= R8
; D 4282 A0 02 9C       IFTRUEI PNFMT
; D 4285 B0 02 91       GAL PNSCI
; PNNEG:
; D 4288 11 0E 00 74    LOADXI R14 0074                    e < 0: plain if e >= -12
; D 428C 88 3E          TESTGXY R3 >= R14
; D 428E A0 02 9C       IFTRUEI PNFMT
; PNSCI:
; D 4291 11 06 00 01    LOADXI R6 0001                     Otherwise d.ddddddd E x
; D 4295 23 00 89       COPYXY R8 -> R9
; D 4298 11 08 00 81    LOADXI R8 0081
; PNFMT:
; D 429C 11 0E 00 80    LOADXI R14 0080
; D 42A0 88 E8          TESTGXY R14 >= R8                  p <= 0: 0. and zeros first
; D 42A2 A1 02 B5       IFFALSEI PNDS
; D 42A5 CA 30          SEROUTI 30 '0'
; D 42A7 CA 2E          SEROUTI 2E '.'
; PNZ:
; D 42A9 87 8E          TESTXY R8 = R14
; D 42AB A0 02 B5       IFTRUEI PNDS
; D 42AE CA 30          SEROUTI 30 '0'
; D 42B0 42 08          INCX R8
; D 42B2 B0 02 A9       GAL PNZ
; PNDS:
; D 42B5 23 00 8A       COPYXY R8 -> R10
; D 42B8 53 0A 00 80    SUBXI R10 0080                     RA = digits before the point
; D 42BC 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; PNL:
; D 42C0 87 47          TESTXY R4 = R7                     Printed them all?
; D 42C2 A0 02 E5       IFTRUEI PNTAIL
; D 42C5 2E 04 0D 02    READIDX R4 0D02
; D 42C9 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 42CC C9             SEROUT
; D 42CD 42 04          INCX R4
; D 42CF 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 42D1 A0 02 C0       IFTRUEI PNL
; D 42D4 43 0A          DECX R10
; D 42D6 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 42D8 A1 02 C0       IFFALSEI PNL
; D 42DB 87 47          TESTXY R4 = R7                     the point, if digits follow
; D 42DD A0 02 C0       IFTRUEI PNL
; D 42E0 CA 2E          SEROUTI 2E '.'
; D 42E2 B0 02 C0       GAL PNL
; PNTAIL:
; D 42E5 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10                         Zeros to fill an integer out
; D 42E7 A0 02 F1       IFTRUEI PNEXP
; D 42EA CA 30          SEROUTI 30 '0'
; D 42EC 43 0A          DECX R10
; D 42EE B0 02 E5       GAL PNTAIL
; PNEXP:
; D 42F1 8C 06          TESTXZ R6
; D 42F3 A0 03 21       IFTRUEI PNRET
; D 42F6 CA 45          SEROUTI 45 'E'
; D 42F8 43 09          DECX R9                            x = p - 1
; D 42FA 11 0E 00 80    LOADXI R14 0080
; D 42FE 89 9E          TESTLXY R9 < R14
; D 4300 A1 03 0B       IFFALSEI PNEP
; D 4303 CA 2D          SEROUTI 2D '-'
; D 4305 51 E9 09       SUBXYZ R14 - R9 -> R9
; D 4308 B0 03 0F       GAL PNEV
; PNEP:
; D 430B 53 09 00 80    SUBXI R9 0080
; PNEV:
; D 430F 4D 9F          DIVXY R9 / R15
; D 4311 25             COPYMAA
; D 4312 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4315 A0 03 1C       IFTRUEI PNEU
; D 4318 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 431B C9             SEROUT
; PNEU:
; D 431C 27             COPYREMA
; D 431D 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4320 C9             SEROUT
; PNRET:
; D 4321 BE 00          RETURN
; PNZERO:
; D 4323 CA 30          SEROUTI 30 '0'
; D 4325 BE 00          RETURN

; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; NATIVE CODE  -  a18 listing of Firmware-Math/calc8_native.asm
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;                   R2      EQU     2
;                   R3      EQU     3
;                   R5      EQU     5
;                   R7      EQU     7
;                   R8      EQU     8
;                   R9      EQU     9
;                   R11     EQU     11
;                   R13     EQU     13
;                   R14     EQU     14
;                   R15     EQU     15
;                   CALL    EQU     0D4H            ; SEP R4 - SCRT call, address follows
;                   RETN    EQU     0D5H            ; SEP R5 - SCRT return
;                   DPAGE   EQU     04DH            ; every data address below is in this page
;                   NA      EQU     04D00H          ; STELLAR-relative $0D00
;                   NB      EQU     04D10H          ; $0D10
;                   ANS     EQU     04D20H          ; $0D20  (STELLAR side only)
;                   OPB     EQU     04D30H          ; operation letter
;                   STAT    EQU     04D31H          ; result status
;                   RAWE    EQU     04D32H          ; parser: exponent + $80 of the raw digits
;                   RAWN    EQU     04D33H          ; parser: how many raw digits
;                   RAWS    EQU     04D34H          ; parser: sign
;                   SGN     EQU     04D35H          ; the sign NORM gives its result
;                   W       EQU     04D40H          ; 64-byte digit work area ($4D40-$4D7F)
;                   RDV     EQU     04D80H          ; divide: the running remainder, 9 digits
;                   DVS     EQU     04D90H          ; divide: the divisor, 9 digits (leading 0)
; 4800 F8 4D        ENTRY:  LDI     DPAGE
; 4802 B7                   PHI     R7
; 4803 B8                   PHI     R8
; 4804 BF                   PHI     R15
; 4805 F8 31                LDI     LOW STAT
; 4807 A8                   PLO     R8
; 4808 F8 00                LDI     0
; 480A 58                   STR     R8              ; STAT = 0
; 480B F8 30                LDI     LOW OPB
; 480D A8                   PLO     R8
; 480E 08                   LDN     R8
; 480F FB 4E                XRI     'N'
; 4811 C2 48 2B             LBZ     DON
; 4814 08                   LDN     R8
; 4815 FB 2A                XRI     '*'
; 4817 C2 48 F2             LBZ     DOMUL
; 481A 08                   LDN     R8
; 481B FB 2F                XRI     '/'
; 481D C2 49 36             LBZ     DODIV
; 4820 08                   LDN     R8
; 4821 FB 2D                XRI     '-'
; 4823 C2 48 5B             LBZ     DOSUB
; 4826 C0 48 62             LBR     DOADD
; 4829 E2           DONE:   SEX     R2
; 482A D5                   DB      RETN            ; home to the RUNMC handler
; 482B F8 34        DON:    LDI     LOW RAWS
; 482D A7                   PLO     R7
; 482E F8 35                LDI     LOW SGN
; 4830 A8                   PLO     R8
; 4831 07                   LDN     R7
; 4832 58                   STR     R8              ; SGN = RAWS
; 4833 F8 33                LDI     LOW RAWN
; 4835 A7                   PLO     R7
; 4836 07                   LDN     R7
; 4837 AB                   PLO     R11             ; L = the digit count
; 4838 FC 40                ADI     LOW W
; 483A A8                   PLO     R8              ; W[L] ...
; 483B F8 0A                LDI     10
; 483D A9                   PLO     R9
; 483E F8 00        DON1:   LDI     0               ; ... W[L+9] = 0: what NORM reads past the end
; 4840 58                   STR     R8
; 4841 18                   INC     R8
; 4842 29                   DEC     R9
; 4843 89                   GLO     R9
; 4844 3A 3E                BNZ     DON1
; 4846 F8 32                LDI     LOW RAWE
; 4848 A7                   PLO     R7
; 4849 07                   LDN     R7
; 484A FC 80                ADI     080H            ; E = RAWE - $80 + $8000
; 484C AD                   PLO     R13
; 484D F8 7F                LDI     07FH
; 484F 7C 00                ADCI    0
; 4851 BD                   PHI     R13
; 4852 F8 10                LDI     LOW NB
; 4854 AF                   PLO     R15
; 4855 D4                   DB      CALL
; 4856 4A 7C                DW      NORM
; 4858 C0 48 29             LBR     DONE
; 485B F8 10        DOSUB:  LDI     LOW NB
; 485D A8                   PLO     R8
; 485E 08                   LDN     R8
; 485F FB 01                XRI     1
; 4861 58                   STR     R8
; 4862 F8 12        DOADD:  LDI     LOW NB+2
; 4864 A7                   PLO     R7
; 4865 07                   LDN     R7
; 4866 C2 48 29             LBZ     DONE            ; adding zero: A stands
; 4869 F8 02                LDI     LOW NA+2
; 486B A7                   PLO     R7
; 486C 07                   LDN     R7
; 486D 3A 82                BNZ     ADD1
; 486F F8 10                LDI     LOW NB          ; A is zero: the answer is B
; 4871 A7                   PLO     R7
; 4872 F8 00                LDI     LOW NA
; 4874 A8                   PLO     R8
; 4875 F8 0A                LDI     10
; 4877 A9                   PLO     R9
; 4878 47           ADD0:   LDA     R7
; 4879 58                   STR     R8
; 487A 18                   INC     R8
; 487B 29                   DEC     R9
